{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1054643-2e-how-to-rise-pilgrimage-trait","id":1054643,"title":"[2E] How to rise Pilgrimage Trait?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-24T21:56:51-08:00","id":1054643,"title":"[2E] How to rise Pilgrimage Trait?","content":"I'm running Promethean PC in our Boston game for few session now and he still has Pilgrimage Trait on 1 dot. How should it be risen? I made something wrong in my ST ways? Here are helping questions:<br /> <br /> 1. Can I - as ST - just declare 'You Pilgrimage is rising in you, take next dot of it'? Or should players always invest in it?<br /> 2. Can Pilgrimage just rise after some very large Milestone, on itself?<br /> 3. If I remember, there are 3 Milestones 'importance', each giving different amount of Vitriol<span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Beats, 1, 3 and 5 ( i.e. 1 Vitriol Experience ), yes?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">4. If 2 is yes, how various Milestones: U</span></span></span>niversal, Prescribed and Instinctive - are 'costly/important' in Vitriol Beats?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T22:16:13-08:00","id":1054646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1054643-2e-how-to-rise-pilgrimage-trait#post1054643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Can I - as ST - just declare 'You Pilgrimage is rising in you, take next dot of it'? Or should players always invest in it?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the character is in fact a player character? No. You can toss a gimme milestone in their path and hope they take the opportunity.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Can Pilgrimage just rise after some very large Milestone, on itself? </div> </div> </div>That is, in fact, the primary benefit of a superlative milestone relative to the lesser varieties \u2014 you don't have to spend Vitriol Experiences to raise your Pilgrimage rating at a superlative milestone (and in fact you can't, because that'd be double-dipping).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. If I remember, there are 3 Milestones 'importance', each giving different amount of Vitriol Beats, 1, 3 and 5 ( i.e. 1 Vitriol Experience ), yes? </div> </div> </div>Minor milestones give 1-3 Vitriol Beats, major milestones give a Vitriol Experience, superlative milestones give a Vitriol Experience and a step forward on the Pilgrimage.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. If 2 is yes, how various Milestones: Universal, Prescribed and Instinctive - are 'costly/important' in Vitriol Beats? </div> </div> </div>Milestone magnitude has virtually no correlation to milestone type except for completing roles and dying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-25-2017, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-24T22:17:54-08:00","id":1054647,"title":"","content":"Pg 184 is what you are looking for. Your are right in the idea, but the numbers are off. Minor milestones give between 1-3 Vitrol beats, a major milestone gives a Vitrol <b>experience </b>, and a superlative milestone give a Vitrol experience and raises Pilgramage by one. Completing roles that are part of the pilgrimage are superlative, as is dying drinking from one of the rivers of the underworld. Completing roles not on the pilgramage is a major milestone. All other milestones are subject to ST discretion, so if you judge the Promethean has hit a superlative milestone, their pilgramage goes up automatically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T00:19:57-08:00","id":1054672,"title":"","content":"Would first Torment event ending in suicide attempt by Created ( even when saved by mages from dying) be Superlative Milestone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T09:31:00-08:00","id":1054798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1054643-2e-how-to-rise-pilgrimage-trait?p=1054672#post1054672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would first Torment event ending in suicide attempt by Created ( even when saved by mages from dying) be Superlative Milestone?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible, but some more context on what happened would be helpful. The role the Promethean occupies could very well change the answer. Was there a choice the Promethean was presented with that made them choose to attempt suicide? Pg 298 provides guidence on the magnitudes of milestones. It may be helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T09:53:20-08:00","id":1054813,"title":"","content":"Suicide attempt was Torment act based on our Tammuz PC rebelling against him beeing obejctified by mages around him. Interesting, there is almost literal example in this Milestone creation advises on page 298.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PtC 2E p. 298</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A major instinctive milestone is a turning point where the character makes a concrete decision. A Tammuz, made to be an obedient servant, has a minor milestone when asked to choose what\u2019s for dinner or where to go on a day trip. A major milestone then focuses on a significant decision that affects the future: does the throng try to find the Athanor in the Minnesota forests or hunt down the Centimani operating in Cleveland? Making a decision of that magnitude is a major milestone.<br /> <br /> Superlative milestones go one further. The same character has issues with needing to decide for himself, but also with rebelling against authority \u2014 he doesn\u2019t want anyone to tell him what to do again. His Storyteller decides to give him a choice. Neither outcome is bad, but the obviously better choice involves following the orders of someone that the character doesn\u2019t like. Will he buckle down and do as he\u2019s told, or take the other option out of a rebellious streak? Whichever he chooses is a significant statement about his character.</div> </div> </div> </div>From this description seems that mine players PC <i>should</i> get Superlative Milestone here. So thanks on this advise! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> When character is changing Refinements based on actions and goals of character after this Superlative Milestone - Will Refinement shift be <b>another</b> Superlative or Major Milestone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}